        "oldValue": "An opera adaptation of George Saunders' Booker Prize-winning novel set in a supernatural afterlife realm. Lincoln in the Bardo takes place in the bardo, a transitional plane between death and rebirth populated by spirits who resist accepting their fate. The story centers on 11-year-old Willie, the recently deceased son of Abraham Lincoln, whose father's grief-stricken visits to his tomb keep Willie's spirit tethered to the bardo rather than allowing him to move on. A community of bardo residents bands together to help free Willie, navigating the boundary between the living world and what comes after. The opera is composed by Missy Mazzoli, with a libretto by Royce Vavrek, based on George Saunders' Booker Prize-winning novel. The production is conducted by Yannick Nézet-Séguin and direct...",
